FerrionOS change to upstream userutils (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 641a5aa81574db79d883151bc3438d3e59f90b88 after the existing recipe patches.

Add -S to sudo so a non-interactive caller can authenticate by passing one password line on standard input. The password is read directly from file descriptor 0 one byte at a time up to MAX_STDIN_PASSWORD_BYTES (1024 bytes), stopping immediately at the newline so any remaining bytes on standard input stay aligned for the executed command, and wiped via WipedString and wipe_bytes after use. Without -S, sudo keeps its existing refusal when standard input is not a terminal.

